---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---
<Layout title="Investor Resources | broker pal" description="Practical real estate investor guides, property due diligence checklists, financing basics, and tools from broker pal.">
<div class="resources">
  <section class="resource-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">broker pal · INVESTOR RESOURCE CENTER</p>
    <h1>Better information for your next investment.</h1>
    <p class="intro">A practical starting point for evaluating an investment property, understanding financing options, and preparing for the next conversation. Use the guides and tools below to organize your questions and compare the details that matter.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="/tools">Explore investor tools <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/apply">Discuss a property with broker pal →</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="resource-section">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">START WITH THE NUMBERS</p><h2>Investor tools</h2><p>Use the information you have today. Clearly distinguish your assumptions from verified property and lender information.</p></div>
    <div class="tool-grid">
      <a class="tool-card featured" href="/tools/property-report"><span class="tag">PROPERTY RESEARCH</span><h3>Investment Property Report</h3><p>Organize an address, property details, your assumptions, available public data, and an estimated value when a supported source returns one.</p><b>Build a property report <span>↗</span></b></a>
      <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/dscr-calculator"><span class="tag">RENTAL ANALYSIS</span><h3>DSCR Calculator</h3><p>Explore how entered rental income, operating expenses, and monthly debt service affect an estimated coverage ratio and cash flow.</p><b>Calculate a scenario <span>↗</span></b></a>
      <a class="tool-card" href="/tools/loan-comparison"><span class="tag">FINANCING REVIEW</span><h3>Loan Comparison</h3><p>Compare two entered scenarios side by side, including estimated principal and interest, closing costs, down payment, and prepayment terms.</p><b>Compare loan scenarios <span>↗</span></b></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="resource-section alt">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">KNOW THE FINANCING PATHS</p><h2>Investment financing basics</h2><p>Different properties and business plans call for different financing conversations. Program availability, qualification, terms, and documentation depend on the lender and the transaction.</p></div>
    <div class="guide-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>DSCR rental loans</h3><p>Debt service coverage ratio (DSCR) financing evaluates a rental property's income in relation to its qualifying debt service. Understand the rent assumptions, expenses, taxes, insurance, association dues, and the lender's calculation method.</p><a href="/#loan-programs">Explore DSCR financing →</a></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Fix &amp; flip financing</h3><p>Short-term financing for an investment property renovation or resale strategy. Before pursuing a project, map the acquisition cost, repair scope, contingency, timeline, carrying costs, and realistic exit plan.</p><a href="/#loan-programs">Explore fix &amp; flip options →</a></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Bridge financing</h3><p>Bridge financing may be considered when timing matters or a borrower needs interim financing. Review the expected term, extension provisions, repayment strategy, costs, and what happens if the exit takes longer than planned.</p><a href="/#loan-programs">Explore bridge options →</a></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Commercial &amp; business-purpose loans</h3><p>Commercial and business-purpose financing can involve property cash flow, business use, collateral, borrower structure, and a lender's specific underwriting criteria. Confirm the intended use and eligibility before relying on a proposed structure.</p><a href="/#loan-programs">Explore commercial financing →</a></article>
      <article><span>05</span><h3>ITIN loan programs</h3><p>Some financing programs may consider eligible applicants using an Individual Taxpayer Identification Number. Requirements vary by lender and program; ask about identification, income, credit, assets, property, and occupancy rules that apply.</p><a href="/#loan-programs">Learn about ITIN programs →</a></article>
      <article><span>06</span><h3>Compare the full loan terms</h3><p>Do not evaluate a financing proposal by interest rate alone. Compare points and fees, cash to close, reserves, amortization, interest-only periods, prepayment penalties, maturity, and extension terms.</p><a href="/tools/loan-comparison">Open the loan comparison tool →</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="resource-section">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU MAKE AN OFFER</p><h2>Property due diligence checklist</h2><p>A first-look checklist to help structure your research. It is not a substitute for independent inspections, title work, legal advice, or confirmation with local authorities.</p></div>
    <div class="checklist">
      <article><h3>Property &amp; ownership</h3><ul><li>Confirm the property address, parcel identification, legal description, and current ownership through authoritative records.</li><li>Review title, liens, easements, access, taxes, and any recorded restrictions with the appropriate professionals.</li><li>Confirm zoning, permitted use, legal unit count, permits, rental registration, and local licensing requirements.</li></ul></article>
      <article><h3>Condition &amp; operating costs</h3><ul><li>Review inspection findings, roof and major systems, deferred maintenance, and contractor estimates.</li><li>Obtain realistic property tax, insurance, utilities, association dues, management, and maintenance figures.</li><li>Check flood exposure and determine whether additional insurance or mitigation may be required.</li></ul></article>
      <article><h3>Income &amp; exit strategy</h3><ul><li>Support rent assumptions with current comparable rentals and review leases, occupancy, deposits, and concessions.</li><li>Model vacancy, repairs, capital expenses, operating costs, and debt service—not just gross rent.</li><li>Stress-test the hold, refinance, sale, or other repayment plan if rates, costs, rents, or timing change.</li></ul></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="resource-section alt">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A FEW TERMS WORTH KNOWING</p><h2>Investor glossary</h2></div>
    <div class="glossary">
      <div><b>DSCR</b><p>Debt service coverage ratio. A measure comparing qualifying property income with qualifying debt service. The exact calculation varies by lender.</p></div>
      <div><b>NOI</b><p>Net operating income. Property income after operating expenses, generally before debt service and income taxes.</p></div>
      <div><b>LTV</b><p>Loan-to-value. The loan amount divided by the value used by the lender for its calculation.</p></div>
      <div><b>PITIA</b><p>Principal, interest, taxes, insurance, and association dues. A common housing-cost grouping; lender calculations may differ.</p></div>
      <div><b>Prepayment penalty</b><p>A contract term that may impose a charge if a loan is paid off or paid down early, as defined in the loan documents.</p></div>
      <div><b>Cash to close</b><p>The funds expected to be needed to complete the transaction, including the down payment and applicable closing costs, credits, and adjustments.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="resource-cta">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT STEP</p><h2>Have a property or financing question?</h2><p>Bring the property details and the questions you want answered. broker pal can help you explore potential financing paths and identify what information is needed next.</p></div>
    <div class="cta-actions"><a class="button primary" href="/apply">Start a loan inquiry <span>↗</span></a><a class="button outline" href="/community">Explore Opportunity Circle <span>↗</span></a></div>
  </section>
  <p class="disclaimer">Educational information only. Tools and examples provide estimates and general research, not an appraisal, tax or legal advice, a rate quote, loan approval, or a commitment to lend. Data may be incomplete or unavailable. Verify property information, program eligibility, and all financing terms with the appropriate sources and professionals. Loan terms are subject to lender guidelines, underwriting, and approval.</p>
</div>
</Layout>
<style>
:global(body){background:#002447;color:#f4f8fb}
.resources{background:#f5f8fa;color:#24394d}
.resource-hero{padding:68px max(24px,calc((100% - 1120px)/2)) 62px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#002447,#0c3b58);color:#f7fbff}
.eyebrow{font-size:10px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#18d0d0;margin:0 0 14px}
.resource-hero h1{max-width:820px;font-size:clamp(40px,5.2vw,64px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-2px;color:#fff;margin:0 0 20px}
.intro{max-width:780px;color:#d2e0e8;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;margin:0}
.hero-actions{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:28px}
.button{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:13px 20px;border-radius:28px;text-decoration:none;font-size:14px;font-weight:800}
.primary{background:#18d0d0;color:#002447}.primary:hover{background:#65e6e1}
.text-link{color:#d9f8f6;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;font-size:14px}
.resource-section{max-width:1160px;margin:auto;padding:62px 26px}
.resource-section.alt{max-width:none;background:#eaf1f4;padding-left:max(26px,calc((100% - 1108px)/2));padding-right:max(26px,calc((100% - 1108px)/2))}
.section-heading{max-width:780px;margin-bottom:28px}
.section-heading h2{font-size:clamp(30px,3.6vw,43px);line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-1.2px;color:#092b49;margin:0 0 10px}
.section-heading>p:last-child{color:#63778a;line-height:1.7;margin:0}
.tool-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}
.tool-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;min-height:240px;padding:24px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d7e3e9;border-top:4px solid #18bfc0;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 8px 24px #0024470b}
.tool-card.featured{background:#edf7f7;border-top-color:#002447}
.tag{font-size:10px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:1.4px;color:#078e98}
.tool-card h3{font-size:22px;color:#092b49;margin:13px 0 8px}
.tool-card p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;color:#607589;margin:0 0 20px}
.tool-card b{margin-top:auto;color:#078e98;font-size:13px}
.guide-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}
.guide-grid article,.checklist article{background:#fff;border:1px solid #d9e4e9;padding:24px}
.guide-grid article>span{font-size:12px;font-weight:900;color:#0b9ca4}
.guide-grid h3,.checklist h3{font-size:20px;color:#092b49;margin:8px 0}
.guide-grid p,.checklist li{font-size:13px;line-height:1.75;color:#607589}
.guide-grid a{display:inline-block;margin-top:6px;color:#078e98;font-size:13px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none}
.checklist{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}
.checklist ul{padding-left:18px;margin:12px 0 0}
.checklist li{margin:0 0 9px}
.glossary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}
.glossary>div{background:#fff;border-left:3px solid #18bfc0;padding:17px 20px}
.glossary b{font-size:15px;color:#092b49}
.glossary p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.65;color:#607589;margin:5px 0 0}
.resource-cta{max-width:1108px;margin:0 auto 34px;padding:34px;background:#002b4b;color:#fff;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:24px}
.resource-cta .eyebrow{color:#18d0d0}
.resource-cta h2{font-size:clamp(27px,3vw,36px);line-height:1.12;color:#fff;margin:0 0 10px}
.resource-cta p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:620px;color:#d0dfe7;line-height:1.7;margin:0}
.cta-actions{display:grid;gap:10px;flex:0 0 auto}
.button.outline{border:1px solid #75bfc4;color:#e6f8f7;justify-content:center}
.disclaimer{max-width:1108px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 0 42px;color:#748698;font-size:11px;line-height:1.7}
@media(max-width:850px){.tool-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.checklist{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.resource-cta{margin-left:24px;margin-right:24px;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start}.disclaimer{padding-left:24px;padding-right:24px}}
@media(max-width:600px){.resource-hero{padding:48px 22px}.resource-hero h1{font-size:42px}.intro{font-size:16px}.resource-section,.resource-section.alt{padding:44px 20px}.tool-grid,.guide-grid,.checklist,.glossary{grid-template-columns:1fr}.tool-card{min-height:0}.resource-cta{margin:0 20px 25px;padding:25px}.disclaimer{padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px}}
</style>